From 0b507dcbc73ad337a326c3b2c639e231e75ab55d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Audia <therealgraysky@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 04:36:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: bump 6.18 to 6.18.65

- New symbol RTC_HCTOSYS_TIME32_LIMIT disabled in generic config since userspace is
  time64 and enabling it would reject RTC dates past 2038.
- mac80211: use the ns_common wiphy_namespace() on 6.18.65+, which backported the
  class namespace change to stable.
- Changelog: https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/ChangeLog-6.18.65

Removed upstreamed:
  linux/generic/backport-6.18/500-v6.19-ksmbd-server-avoid-busy-polling-in-accept-loop.patch[1]
